Licensing for tools/
=====================

The tools in this directory are NOT all under the same license. See the
repository-root LICENSE for the authoritative map. Every directory here is
named below; a tool that appears in neither list is an omission, not a
permission.

Where the line falls: Apache-2.0 covers what is needed to ESTABLISH CONFORMANCE
with the format and to verify this distribution. FSL covers everything that
reads a model for a purpose other than validating it - building its graph,
naming what its edges mean, judging whether it says enough, querying it,
allocating into its id space, rendering it. Those are positions about what a
good model is, not properties of the format.

Apache License, Version 2.0 - see ../LICENSE-APACHE

  - validator/              the reference conformance validator
  - doc-snippet-validate/   validates the YAML examples inside the docs
  - port/                   verifies the shipped files against the manifest
                            published with them; it describes no blueprint and
                            reads no model
  - vscode-blueprint/       the editor navigation extension
                            (see its own vscode-blueprint/LICENSE)

  Free to use, modify and redistribute, including in commercial and proprietary
  products. Conformance belongs with the format: a schema whose only complete
  definition is a tool you cannot freely run is not an open format.

Functional Source License 1.1 (ALv2 Future License) - see ../LICENSE-FSL

  - model-builder/          the model graph, and the vocabulary typing its edges
  - semantic-checker/       the semantic rule pack
  - quality-gate/           self-description coverage
  - coverage-check/         drift between a model's code_refs and the source tree
  - model-query/            the reuse audit over a built model
  - entity-query/           search before you mint
  - next-id/                typed id allocation
  - build-stamp/            build identity for generated artifacts
  - renderer/               markdown and Mermaid documents
  - schema-update/          versioned model migrations
  - schema-atlas/           the generated schema reference
  - guide-publisher/        the guide atlas, built for publication

  Free for any Permitted Purpose (internal use, non-commercial education and
  research, and professional services you provide to others). NOT for a
  Competing Use. Each version converts to Apache-2.0 two years after release.

  The rule ENGINE is not in this directory and is not covered here: it is the
  separate Apache-2.0 package @archally/semantic-checker. What is licensed above
  is the blueprint rule set and the adapter - the opinions, not the machinery.
